# Every file in this repository is text, stored and checked out with LF
# endings on every OS - whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine.
#
# Why: on Windows, autocrlf=true checked these files out with CRLF. The Node
# scripts didn't care, but tooling that edits them did: exact-match edits on
# multi-line text silently missed, and one script that split on "\n" and
# re-joined mangled a whole file. The eval scaffolds are bash, which reads a
# CRLF line's trailing "\r" as part of the command. And a checkout that
# differs by OS makes "the same file" hash differently on two machines.
# PowerShell 5.1 and Windows editors read LF without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf
